From 9cdb75989fc70cef0734c0bb89eb48e23569c1a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 12:24:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove Engines/rl_ppo_adaptive.py -- dead, misleading PPO
 module

Flagged by an independent repository review (24 Jul 2026, commit
67eea1d9): PPORouter claimed to be PPO but implemented none of it --
fixed random weights from a hardcoded seed (815), no training loop,
same output every run. Its own module docstring already said as much
("NOT a training implementation of PPO"), and Engines/README.md
(written 23 Jul) already documented the gap.

Removed rather than relabeled, after confirming via a repo-wide
search that nothing real depended on it:
- Not imported by production_harness.py, sentinel_worker.py, or any
  live path.
- Not used by the real simulator (iceberg_complete_simulator.py),
  which already uses Engines/simple_rl_trainer.py's SimpleRLTrainer --
  a smaller module that does genuinely train (REINFORCE-style policy
  gradient with a value baseline).
- Its only real consumer was one test (test_critical_integration.py)
  asserting a constructor argument got stored -- removed alongside it.
- Sim/Simulator.py mentions 'PPORouter' only in a historical design
  comment (cross-engine output-format normalization), not an import.

Engines/README.md updated to record the removal and point to
SimpleRLTrainer as the actual starting point if real PPO (or
anything beyond it) is wanted later. Tests/test_all_suites.py's
summary print strings corrected to match.

442 passed, 6 skipped (443 baseline - 1 removed test), twice
back-to-back. ruff clean, bandit -ll clean.
